Verification of the Max PRB for load metric algorithm within PRB Pooling Report
    [Documentation]     Verify the L1 SubPool ID=0 capacity within PRB Pooling Allocation SubPool Reports for 20Mhz bandwith
    ...   Dl L1SubPoolStreamPrbCapacity (1 subpool Max Num Stream PRB) = 1272*30%= = 414 PRB;
    ...   Dl NumMinStreamPrb is the sum of streamPRB.min for all cell: 48 Prbbmin * 2 (conversion A2 prb->stream) *2 (cells) = 192
    ...   Dl NumMaxStreamPrb is the sum of streamPRB.max for all cell: 106 Prbmax * 2 (conversion DL A2 prb->stream) *2 (cells) = 424
    ...   Dl NumAllocStreamPrb1 is the streamPRB allocated for selected cell (round robin) : set to 0 in LB
    ...   Dl NumAllocStreamPrb2 is the streamPRB allocated globaly for all the other cell (Load Based) :
    ...   NumAllocStreamPrb2 = 106prbmax * 2 (conversion DL A2 prb->stream) *2 (cells) = 414
    ...   It is assumed that NIDD FddNrCellConfigTradeoff is set to max cells (feature CB6913)
    [Arguments]
